    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:5a4836cca1208c95",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "mode": "word_span",
      "text": "Day 1 · Meeting at the airport and transfer to your hotel. Then depart for the ceremonial centre of Orongo. Climb the slopes of the Rano Kau volcano to a viewpoint on the edge of the crater, which holds a beautiful lake with its characteristic vegetation.\n\nVisit the ceremonial village of Orongo, where the island’s chief was chosen for a whole year through a perilous competition: every spring, the clans gathered in its stone houses, awaiting the arrival of the sacred Manutara bird to choose the Tangata Manu, the Birdman. Duration: 4 hours.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1zUNi_nTIgTJ0v2CQiDYg3A4tsff1HaQ5",
        "revision": "2026-10-22T14:03:05.061Z",
        "documentSha256": "e8797275b1b80fec09e917a42a64128fccde97924b970f75f592f0cbcb149492",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
            "ref": "word/document.xml#p0066",
            "textSha256": "8f4c4dd0d8896941267513b757a15d8263fd58d3ebcc2b217599b8836be34855"
          },
          {
            "ref": "word/document.xml#p0067",
            "textSha256": "048b555fc680be79d5f002ecefba95638a8cfa7a6dc8aac98090cf1629f7df98"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_title:ca0a4d6daf445776",
      "field": "itinerary.title",
      "mode": "word_span",
      "text": "The land of the Moai",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1zUNi_nTIgTJ0v2CQiDYg3A4tsff1HaQ5",
        "revision": "2026-10-22T14:03:05.061Z",
        "documentSha256": "e8797275b1b80fec09e917a42a64128fccde97924b970f75f592f0cbcb149492",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
            "ref": "word/document.xml#p0074",
            "textSha256": "d82a39223fb0c05f65310015720b9d66555f68d899df364ccfc8457a7a44a1b0"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:569e72e117968fcc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "mode": "word_span",
      "text": "Day 2 · Breakfast, then a full-day tour of the island. Along the south coast, see unrestored platforms: Ahu Vaihu in Hanga Te’e Bay and Akahanga, said to be the burial place of the legendary king Hotu Matua. Continue to Rano Raraku, the quarry where most of the Moai were carved: of the nearly 900 statues on the island, some 397 still lie or stand on the slopes of this extinct volcano. Box lunch in nature.\n\nVisit Ahu Tongariki, the largest platform on the island, with 15 restored Moai, then drive east to Ahu Te Pito Kura and the “Navel of the World”. End at Anakena Beach, with its warm turquoise water, white sand, palm trees and the Ahu Nau Nau platform, one of the most beautiful landscapes on the island: time for a walk and a swim. Return to Hanga Roa through the centre of the island.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1zUNi_nTIgTJ0v2CQiDYg3A4tsff1HaQ5",
        "revision": "2026-10-22T14:03:05.061Z",
        "documentSha256": "e8797275b1b80fec09e917a42a64128fccde97924b970f75f592f0cbcb149492",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
