    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:4b5ff9b4a37f43cc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "mode": "word_span",
      "text": "Day 3 · Breakfast, then drive to the restored Ahu Akivi platform in the centre of the island, whose seven Moai are said to represent the seven explorers sent to Rapa Nui by King Hotu Matua. See the unrestored Ahu Hanga Puku Riki, then visit Puna Pau, a green and picturesque site whose red tuff, quarried from the slope of the extinct volcano, was used to carve the topknots of the stone giants.\n\nEnd at the Tahai ceremonial complex, with its three platforms from north to south: Ko Te Riku, with restored eyes, Tahai and Vai Uri, part of Rapa Nui National Park, a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Duration: 4 hours. Transfer to the airport.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
